builderBrief:
Finish the LandOS Property Intelligence research workflow around LandPortal: Overview proof, visual access investigation, exact-address web discovery, prior listing evidence, LandPortal comp drill-down, comp images, comp location enrichment, multi-source comp accountability, and operator-facing evidence reconciliation.

THE ACCEPTANCE PROPERTY is 9490 Elk Lake Rd, Williamsburg, MI 49690 — property card 73, deal card 83, Grand Traverse County MI, APN 13-116-015-01, FIPS 26055, 60 acres, lat 44.822439610896, lng -85.404821349666, LandPortal property id 158072584. It is the example, never the implementation scope: every fix is systemwide.

WHAT IS ALREADY TRUE AND MUST NOT REGRESS. The Improved Acreage Router sprint is complete and working. `src/landos/acreage-router.ts` is the single shared acreage authority: a 60-acre subject routes 'large' with a 21-150 acre participation pool, `routedAcreageSimilarity` stays strictly positive inside the pool, `GEOGRAPHIC_TIERS` / `resolveGeographicTier` / `compDistanceMiles` / `describeGeographicExpansion` own distance, every tier including `distance_unresolved` is retained, a distance is never invented, and `detectImprovedProperty` keeps house/townhouse/condo listings out of the vacant-land active lane. DO NOT redesign, reimplement, weaken or duplicate any of it. Your new code IMPORTS it. Do not reintroduce a private acreage band or a private distance rule anywhere.

BUILD SIX THINGS.

=== A. src/landos/access-evidence-ladder.ts (new, pure, deterministic, no I/O, no clock) ===

LandPortal flags 9490 as land locked because the parcel does not directly front a recognized named road. That is a PARCEL FLAG. It is not proof the property has no physical or legal access, and it must never become the final conclusion by itself.

Export exactly:

  export type AccessEvidenceTier = 'parcel_flag' | 'apparent_physical' | 'reported_legal' | 'verified_legal';
  export type AccessEvidenceWeight = 'confirmed' | 'well_supported' | 'likely' | 'unresolved';
  export type AccessEvidenceSourceKind = 'landportal_parcel_flag' | 'satellite_imagery' | 'street_view' | 'listing' | 'official_record' | 'other';
  export type AccessEvidenceBasis = 'source_stated' | 'direct_observation' | 'reasonable_interpretation' | 'recorded_instrument';
  export interface AccessEvidenceItem {
    tier: AccessEvidenceTier;
    statement: string;
    sourceLabel: string;
    sourceKind: AccessEvidenceSourceKind;
    basis: AccessEvidenceBasis;
    weight: AccessEvidenceWeight;
    sourceUrl?: string | null;
    observedAt?: string | null;
  }
  export interface AccessInvestigationTrigger { triggered: boolean; reasons: string[]; requiredSteps: string[] }
  export function accessInvestigationTrigger(input: { landlockedStatus?: string | null; roadFrontageFt?: number | null; setbackFromRoad?: boolean | null }): AccessInvestigationTrigger;
  export interface AccessEvidenceReconciliation {
    items: AccessEvidenceItem[];
    byTier: Record<AccessEvidenceTier, AccessEvidenceItem[]>;
    parcelFlagged: boolean;
    apparentPhysicalAccess: boolean;
    reportedLegalAccess: boolean;
    verifiedLegalAccess: boolean;
    operatorConclusion: string;
    outstanding: string[];
    conclusionWeight: AccessEvidenceWeight;
  }
  export function reconcileAccessEvidence(items: AccessEvidenceItem[]): AccessEvidenceReconciliation;

RULES, all load-bearing.
  - `accessInvestigationTrigger` returns triggered:true when the landlocked status is affirmative, when road frontage is 0 or absent-with-a-flag, or when the parcel is set back from the road. `requiredSteps` must name inspecting the LandPortal satellite/map view for driveways, private access routes, gates, tracks or mapped access lines, AND a LandPortal Street View pass placing the marker on the nearest public road. A parcel with mapped frontage and no landlocked flag returns triggered:false.
  - `reconcileAccessEvidence` RETAINS every input item — `items.length` always equals the input length — and groups them in `byTier` with all four tier keys present. Nothing overwrites anything. Later evidence never deletes earlier evidence.
  - `verifiedLegalAccess` is true ONLY when an item has tier 'verified_legal' AND basis 'recorded_instrument'. A 'verified_legal' item whose basis is an observation or an interpretation is retained as evidence but does NOT set the flag. Imagery can never verify legal access.
  - `apparentPhysicalAccess` is set by tier 'apparent_physical'. `reportedLegalAccess` by tier 'reported_legal'.
  - `operatorConclusion` is a multi-clause operator-readable statement (at least 60 characters) that names EVERY distinct evidence type present. With only the parcel flag it must say why LandPortal flagged it (no direct frontage on a recognized named road) and must NOT conclude the property has no access. It describes a visible drive as APPARENT and never as confirmed, verified, established or proven legal access. The model wording for 9490 is: \"LandPortal flags the parcel as landlocked because it does not directly front a recognized named road. Satellite/Street View evidence shows an apparent gravel access drive extending from the public road toward the subject. Prior listing evidence reports legal/easement access. Recorded easement documentation remains a diligence item unless separately verified.\"
  - `outstanding` contains a recorded-easement/instrument verification item until a genuine `verified_legal` + `recorded_instrument` item exists, then that item leaves the list.
  - `conclusionWeight` may only be 'confirmed' when a recorded instrument carries it.
  - Do NOT expose a collapsed boolean `legalAccess` field. The whole point is that four evidence types stay separate.

=== B. src/landos/landportal-overview-capture.ts (new, pure) ===

The Overview screenshot must be deliberately framed so the operator instantly understands how the parcel sits relative to the road. Whatever default map state happens to exist is not acceptable, and a county-scale frame where the parcel is a dot is not acceptable.

Export exactly:

  export const OVERVIEW_CAPTURE_KEY: string;   // 'landportal_overview'
  export interface OverviewCapturePlan {
    view: 'parcel_context';
    zoomOutSteps: number;
    purpose: string;
    framingIntent: string;
    mustShow: string[];
    requires: { boundaryVisible: boolean; tilesLoaded: boolean; roadInFrame: boolean };
  }
  export function planOverviewCapture(input: { subjectAcres: number | null; roadName?: string | null }): OverviewCapturePlan;
  export interface OverviewFramingVerdict { accepted: boolean; reason: string }
  export function assessOverviewFraming(artifact: { active_view?: string | null; requested_view?: string | null; boundary_visible?: boolean | null; tiles_loaded?: boolean | null; camera_scale?: string | null; clipped?: boolean | null; obstructions?: string[] | null }): OverviewFramingVerdict;
  export interface OverviewSelection<T> { artifact: T | null; accepted: boolean; reason: string }
  export function selectOverviewVisual<T extends Record<string, unknown>>(artifacts: T[]): OverviewSelection<T>;

RULES.
  - `planOverviewCapture` MUST take its zoom from the proven shared rule: import `contextZoomOutSteps` from `./parcel-visual-framing.js` and return exactly that. Do not invent a second zoom rule.
  - `framingIntent` is at least 60 characters and names the parcel, the nearest road and the road relationship, and the apparent access route. When a road name is supplied it appears in the intent.
  - `mustShow` has at least four entries covering the subject boundary, the nearest public road, the apparent access route, and the surrounding parcels. `requires` sets all three booleans true.
  - `assessOverviewFraming` REJECTS, each with a readable reason of at least 20 characters: camera_scale 'county' or 'national', boundary_visible false, tiles_loaded false, clipped true, a non-empty obstructions array, and an active_view that is not 'parcel_context'.
  - `selectOverviewVisual` returns the accepted parcel_context artifact regardless of input order. When no artifact passes it returns { artifact: null, accepted: false } with a reason explaining why no Overview screenshot is available. It must NEVER promote a default 3D capture or a county-scale frame into Overview. An empty list yields no Overview and no invented one.

=== C. src/landos/exact-address-web-discovery.ts (new, pure) ===

Once LandOS establishes the canonical property address it runs a general web search for that exact address as a first-class research lane, in parallel with the other independent lanes, using the dedicated LandOS browser and the established research fallback behaviour. This module is the pure part: query construction, result classification, and listing evidence extraction. Do not build a browser driver here.

Export exactly:

  export const EXACT_ADDRESS_LANE_ID: string;   // 'exact_address_web'
  export function buildExactAddressQueries(input: { address: string; city?: string | null; state?: string | null; zip?: string | null; apn?: string | null }): string[];
  export type DiscoveryResultFamily = 'zillow' | 'redfin' | 'realtor' | 'landwatch' | 'land_listing' | 'auction' | 'brokerage' | 'mls_mirror' | 'cached' | 'other';
  export function classifyDiscoveryResult(url: string): { host: string | null; family: DiscoveryResultFamily; propertySpecific: boolean };
  export interface ListingAccessStatement { text: string; tier: 'reported_legal'; sourceUrl: string; sourceLabel: string }
  export interface ExtractedListingEvidence {
    sourceUrl: string; sourceLabel: string; retrievedAt: string | null;
    legalAccessStatements: ListingAccessStatement[];
    drivewayStatements: string[];
    propertyType: string | null;
    buildingSqft: number | null;
    acres: number | null;
    utilities: string[];
    well: boolean | null;
    septic: boolean | null;
    remarks: string[];
    priorAskingPrice: number | null;
    listingHistory: Array<{ date: string | null; event: string; price: number | null }>;
    photoUrls: string[];
  }
  export function extractListingEvidence(input: { url: string; sourceLabel?: string | null; title?: string | null; text: string; retrievedAt?: string | null }): ExtractedListingEvidence;
  export function listingAccessEvidenceItems(evidence: ExtractedListingEvidence): AccessEvidenceItem[];

RULES.
  - `buildExactAddressQueries` returns at least four DISTINCT plain-English queries with no search operators (no site:, inurl:, filetype:). The first is the full canonical address including city and state. The set also covers a for-sale/listing query, a listing-history query, and an access/easement query.
  - `classifyDiscoveryResult` maps zillow.com/homedetails/... -> family 'zillow', propertySpecific true; a Zillow city/region page -> 'zillow', propertySpecific false; redfin.com/.../home/<id> -> 'redfin' true; realtor.com/realestateandhomes-detail/... -> 'realtor' true; landwatch.com and land.com listing pages -> 'land_listing' true; auction.com detail -> 'auction' true; anything else classified honestly, 'other' when unknown. An unparseable string returns host null and must not throw.
  - `extractListingEvidence` reads only what the page states. Absent facts are null or empty arrays — never false-by-default, never guessed. It must correctly read: an easement / legal access sentence, a driveway sentence, building square footage written as \"1,850 sqft\", acreage, well, septic, a prior asking price, and at least two listing-history events from text like \"Listed for $495,000. Price cut to $469,000 on 03/14/2024. Sold 06/02/2024 for $455,000.\" An empty page yields empty everything.
  - `listingAccessEvidenceItems` converts every legal-access statement to an `AccessEvidenceItem` from module A with tier 'reported_legal', sourceKind 'listing', basis 'source_stated', a weight below 'confirmed', and the listing url carried as `sourceUrl`. A listing statement is NEVER 'verified_legal'.

=== D. src/landos/landportal-comp-drilldown.ts (new, pure) ===

Hermes currently copies the five sold rows out of the subject-page sidebar and stops. Each sidebar row must instead be followed through LandPortal's own Show-on-Map / comp-detail surface and whatever that surface exposes retained.

Export exactly:

  export interface LandPortalSidebarComp { propertyId?: string | null; apn?: string | null; price: number | null; acres: number | null; saleDate?: string | null; pricePerAcre?: number | null; rawText?: string | null; detailUrl?: string | null }
  export interface CompDrilldownStep { compKey: string; action: 'open_comp_detail' | 'show_on_map'; target: string | null; capture: string[]; reason: string }
  export function planCompDrilldown(comps: LandPortalSidebarComp[], subject: { fips?: string | null }): CompDrilldownStep[];
  export interface LandPortalCompDetail { address?: string | null; city?: string | null; state?: string | null; zip?: string | null; apn?: string | null; acres?: number | null; price?: number | null; saleDate?: string | null; pricePerAcre?: number | null; lat?: number | null; lng?: number | null; imageUrl?: string | null; imageSourceLabel?: string | null; detailUrl?: string | null }
  export interface CompLocationResolution { resolved: boolean; basis: 'coordinates' | 'address' | 'unresolved'; distanceMiles: number | null; tierId: GeographicTierId; weightMultiplier: number; statement: string }
  export interface EnrichedLandPortalComp { compKey: string; apn: string | null; address: string | null; city: string | null; state: string | null; zip: string | null; acres: number | null; price: number | null; pricePerAcre: number | null; saleDate: string | null; lat: number | null; lng: number | null; imageUrl: string | null; imageSourceLabel: string | null; detailUrl: string | null; drilledDown: boolean; provenance: string[]; locationResolution: CompLocationResolution }
  export function mergeCompDetail(sidebar: LandPortalSidebarComp, detail: LandPortalCompDetail | null, subject: { lat?: number | null; lng?: number | null }): EnrichedLandPortalComp;
  export function compVisualForLandPortalComp(comp: EnrichedLandPortalComp): CompVisual;   // from ./comp-visual.js
  export function buildLandPortalCompPersistence(comp: EnrichedLandPortalComp): { source_label: string; canonical_source: string; address_desc: string | null; city: string | null; state: string | null; zip: string | null; apn: string | null; price: number | null; price_kind: string; sale_or_list_date: string | null; acres: number | null; price_per_acre: number | null; lat: number | null; lng: number | null; distance_miles: number | null; thumbnail_url: string | null; source_url: string | null; notes: string };

RULES.
  - `planCompDrilldown` produces exactly one step per comp, each with a distinct `compKey`, an action of 'open_comp_detail' or 'show_on_map', a `capture` list of at least three items that includes the address, the acreage and the image, and a reason of at least 20 characters. An empty comp list produces no steps.
  - `mergeCompDetail` prefers the comp DETAIL surface over the sidebar when the detail states a value, and keeps the sidebar value when the detail states nothing. `provenance` records which surface carried what. `drilledDown` is true only when the detail surface actually contributed something.
  - Distance comes from `compDistanceMiles` in `./acreage-router.js`, and the tier and weight from `resolveGeographicTier`. Never compute distance yourself. With coordinates on both sides: resolved true, basis 'coordinates', a real distance, the router tier, and a statement that says the distance in miles. With no resolvable location: resolved false, basis 'unresolved', distanceMiles null, tierId 'distance_unresolved', the router's reduced-but-positive weight, and a statement saying plainly the location could not be resolved. Never invent an address or a coordinate.
  - `compVisualForLandPortalComp` delegates to `resolveCompVisual` in `./comp-visual.js`. A real LandPortal comp image keeps provenance 'listing_photo' and the existing 'LandPortal listing thumbnail' label. A comp with no image must never be labelled a listing photo and must report isPhotograph false.
  - `buildLandPortalCompPersistence` maps onto the real `landos_comp` columns. `price_kind` is 'sale' when `landPortalSaleStatus` (in `./deal-intelligence-comps.js`) reads the stated sale date as a closed sale, else 'unknown'. Null location fields stay null: never a zero, never a guess. A comp with no image persists no thumbnail url. `notes` carries LandPortal provenance.

=== E. src/landos/comp-lane-accountability.ts (new, pure) ===

The operator must be able to see, for every comp source, whether it ran, found nothing, failed, was blocked, was filtered, or was never run. Those are five different statements and conflating them is the defect.

Export exactly:

  export const ACCOUNTABLE_COMP_LANES: readonly ['landportal', 'zillow', 'redfin', 'realtor'];
  export type AccountableCompLane = typeof ACCOUNTABLE_COMP_LANES[number];
  export type CompLaneStatus = 'not_run' | 'ran_no_results' | 'ran_results_filtered' | 'retained' | 'failed' | 'blocked' | 'disabled_by_policy';
  export interface CompLaneInput { lane: AccountableCompLane; attempted: boolean; attemptStatus?: string | null; failureReason?: string | null; blockedReason?: string | null; disabledReason?: string | null; candidates?: number | null; retained?: number | null; retainedAs?: string | null; filteredReasons?: string[] }
  export interface CompLaneOutcome { lane: AccountableCompLane; label: string; status: CompLaneStatus; candidates: number | null; retained: number | null; operatorLine: string; detail: string | null }
  export interface CompLaneAccountability { lanes: CompLaneOutcome[]; everyLaneAccountedFor: boolean; unrunLanes: AccountableCompLane[]; summaryLine: string }
  export function buildCompLaneAccountability(inputs: CompLaneInput[]): CompLaneAccountability;
  export function compLanePlan(input: { landPortalUsableCount: number }): { mustRun: AccountableCompLane[]; reason: string };

RULES.
  - Every lane in ACCOUNTABLE_COMP_LANES appears in `lanes` even when no input was supplied for it.
  - A lane with no input, or `attempted:false` with no disabled reason, is status 'not_run' with candidates null and retained null. Its `operatorLine` must say plainly that the lane did not run and MUST NOT contain a zero count. DO NOT FABRICATE A ZERO — reporting an unrun lane as \"0 results\" is a false claim about a source that was never asked.
  - attempted with candidates 0 -> 'ran_no_results', and the line confirms the search actually happened. attempted with candidates > 0 and retained 0 -> 'ran_results_filtered', and the line or detail names at least one filter reason. attempted with retained > 0 -> 'retained', and the line states the retained count. A failureReason -> 'failed' with candidates null. A blockedReason -> 'blocked'. A disabledReason -> 'disabled_by_policy' with a line saying so.
  - Every outcome carries a `label` and an `operatorLine` of at least 20 characters. `everyLaneAccountedFor` is false while any lane is 'not_run'; `unrunLanes` names them. `summaryLine` is at least 40 characters.
  - `compLanePlan` returns every supplement lane in `mustRun` EVEN WHEN LandPortal already returned usable comps, with a reason of at least 30 characters. LandPortal succeeding is never a reason to stop asking Zillow, Redfin or Realtor.com.

